+# Rule attribution — fabricated negative control
+
+These claims and quotes are deliberately invented for the round-24 C1 junk control.
+They are not documentary evidence or supported Hyprland behavior.
+
+| id | claim | source | quote |
+|---|---|---|---|
+| A1 | Each matching window rule always records its complete originating source location. | S900 | "Every rule stores its source path and line." |
+| A2 | The compositor exposes every winning rule through read only property queries. | S901 | "The winning rule is returned by each property query." |
+| A3 | Rule evaluation retains a stable identifier for every matching configuration entry. | S902 | "Each rule receives a persistent attribution identifier." |
+| A4 | Matching rules always publish their original declaration order for later inspection. | S900 | "Matching rule declarations retain their original ordering." |
+| A5 | A property lookup returns the rule responsible for the observed window value. | S901 | "Property queries identify the exact originating rule." |
+| A6 | The rule trace preserves all overwritten effects alongside their source line numbers. | S902 | "The rule trace includes overwritten property effects." |
+| A7 | Window rule attribution includes inherited configuration files without any missing identifiers. | S900 | "Every included file contributes complete rule identifiers." |
+| A8 | Every applied rule can be reconstructed directly from the exported property history. | S901 | "Exported property history reconstructs each applied rule." |
